        {
          "url": "https://assets.fractal-design.com/files/uxzbxy2o/production/6f9ccb3a36843c7b3e696a62dfa5e7370db78da7.pdf",
          "publisher": "fractal",
          "retrievedAt": "2026-10-01",
          "docType": "manual",
          "fields": [
            "radiatorSupport",
            "psu.clearance",
            "driveTrayLayouts"
          ],
          "title": "North User Guide",
          "locator": "p. 7 All-in-one Water Cooling Build; p. 26 PSU length per drive-tray position; p. 33 Water Cooling Radiator Options; p. 34 Front 360 Radiator Limitation"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "field": "makerSizeClass",
          "text": "From Fractal's page data \"cases_size\":\"Regular\", the size its case listing filters by."
        },
        {
          "field": "gpuClearance",
          "text": "From \"Choose a GPU up to 355 mm, or up to 300 mm with a 360 mm front radiator.\" The user guide's sample AIO build (p. 7) shows a 360 x 120 mm front radiator with \"GPU Length: 267 mm (up to 325 mm possible)\"; the product page's stricter 300 mm is kept. Fractal gives no GPU limit with a 120, 140, 240 or 280 mm front radiator."
        },
        {
          "field": "coolerClearance",
          "text": "Fractal's structured value is 145 mm, but its note says \"145 mm with Fan Bracket (Mesh version only) / 170 mm without\". This TG Light SKU has no side fan bracket (\"The mesh version also ships with a fanhub and a fan bracket\"), so its limit is 170 mm."
        },
        {
          "field": "psu.clearance",
          "text": "From Fractal's note \"1 HDD tray: 255 mm max; 2 HDD tray: 155 mm max\" (the user guide p. 4 says the same). The page does not say how many trays are fitted as shipped, so neither limit is unconditional. They are the best cases: the limit for each tray position is in driveTrayLayouts."
        },
        {
          "field": "gpuMaxThicknessMm",
          "text": "No GPU thickness limit is published."
        },
        {
          "field": "radiatorSupport",
          "text": "From the user guide p. 33, \"Water Cooling Radiator Options\": front 120/240/360 \"Radiator width up to 125 mm\", \"Radiator thickness max 55 mm\"; front 140/280 \"up to 151 mm\", \"max 35 mm\"; top 120/240 \"35 mm max\" thick and \"122 mm max\" wide. The guide gives no limit for the rear 120 mm position."
        },
        {
          "field": "radiatorSupport.0",
          "text": "A front 360 mm radiator: the user guide p. 34 gives \"Radiator End tank 30 mm max\" with the tubes up (AIO); an end tank over 30 mm goes tubes down. Its p. 26 table allows a front 360 only with no drive tray at floor position A; with a tray at A, front radiators go up to 280 mm."
        },
        {
          "field": "verticalGpuMount",
          "text": "The product page says nothing about vertical GPU mounting."
        },
        {
          "field": "fanMounts",
          "text": "Front \"3x 120 or 2x 140 mm\", top \"2x 120/140 mm\", rear \"1x 120 mm\"; the TG version lists no side fan mounts."
        },
        {
          "field": "dimensionsMm",
          "text": "From \"Product dimensions (L × W × H) 447 x 215 x 469 mm\"."
        },
        {
          "field": "frontIo",
          "text": "From \"2x USB Type-A 5Gbps, 1x USB Type-C 20Gbps, 1x Audio Jack\" and \"one USB 3.2 Gen 2×2 Type-C\"."
        },
        {
          "field": "driveTrayLayouts",
          "text": "The user guide p. 26 table, \"PSU Length\" and \"Front Radiator\" per tray layout: one tray at A 255 mm (front radiator up to 280 mm), B 215, C 180, D 140, E 155 (360 mm); two trays A+D 140, A+E 155 (280 mm), B+E, C+E 155, D+E 140 (360 mm). The table's middle column, \"3.5 + 2.5\" (a tick or a cross), is not explained in the guide and is not recorded. The guide gives no PSU limit with no tray fitted."
        }
      ]
    },
